---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import {
  flowcastVersion,
  installCommand,
} from '../lib/version';

const repository =
  'https://github.com/chourmovs/JuggleCast-Community';

const updateCommand =
  `sudo /opt/flowcast/scripts/community/update.sh --version ${flowcastVersion}`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Install JuggleCast on Linux with Docker"
  description={`Install JuggleCast Community ${flowcastVersion} on Linux amd64, review ports and Docker socket risk, then verify your first Icecast broadcast.`}
>
  <section class="page container">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        INSTALLATION · {flowcastVersion}
      </p>

      <h1>Install JuggleCast Community</h1>

      <p>
        The current validated installer targets an
        operator-managed Linux amd64 host. Review the
        installer and security model before running it.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Prerequisites</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Linux amd64, Docker Engine and Docker Compose v2
        </li>

        <li>
          2 CPU cores, at least 4 GB RAM and 10 GB free disk
          plus media storage
        </li>

        <li>
          Free TCP ports <strong>8080</strong> for the
          control/player proxy and <strong>8010</strong> for
          direct Icecast access
        </li>

        <li>
          The standard command-line tools required by the
          installer, including <code>curl</code>,
          <code>openssl</code>, <code>tar</code> and
          <code>sha256sum</code>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Run the validated tagged installer</h2>

      <p>
        Current validated Community release:
        <strong><code>{flowcastVersion}</code></strong>.
      </p>

      <pre><code>{installCommand}</code></pre>

      <p>
        The installer does not install Docker. It verifies
        the release archive, writes
        <code>/opt/flowcast</code>, generates a
        mode-<code>0600</code> <code>.env</code>, pulls
        immutable versioned service images and waits for
        service health.
      </p>

      <p>
        An existing installation environment is not silently
        overwritten. Back up before updating or replacing an
        installation.
      </p>

      <aside class="notice">
        <strong>Root-equivalent Docker access</strong>

        <p>
          The standard <code>{flowcastVersion}</code>
          installation enables Docker Control. Mounting the
          Docker socket gives the control container
          effectively root-level authority over the host.
        </p>

        <p>
          Never expose the control interface to untrusted
          users. Pass <code>--no-docker-control</code> to opt
          out. Start, Stop and Restart actions in the
          interface are then unavailable, while the
          Community broadcast path remains usable through
          the normal Compose lifecycle.
        </p>
      </aside>

      <h2>Review the installer first</h2>

      <p>
        For a more conservative installation process, download
        and inspect the tagged script before running it:
      </p>

      <pre><code>{`curl -fsSLO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chourmovs/JuggleCast-Community/v${flowcastVersion}/install.sh
less install.sh
sudo bash install.sh --version ${flowcastVersion}`}</code></pre>

      <h2>Open the interface and broadcast</h2>

      <ol>
        <li>
          Open <code>http://localhost:8080</code>, or the LAN
          address displayed by the installer.
        </li>

        <li>
          Sign in with the locally generated credentials.
        </li>

        <li>
          Import audio that you own or are permitted to store
          and broadcast.
        </li>

        <li>
          Create or select a playlist and configure its
          programming.
        </li>

        <li>
          Start playout when Docker Control is enabled.
        </li>

        <li>
          Listen through
          <code>/listen/test.mp3</code> on the control origin,
          or directly through
          <code>http://HOST:8010/test.mp3</code>.
        </li>

        <li>
          Run the diagnostic command and confirm that it ends
          with <code>RESULT=PASS</code>.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <pre><code>sudo /opt/flowcast/scripts/community/doctor.sh</code></pre>

      <p>
        Follow the
        <a
          href={`${repository}/blob/main/docs/how-to/first-broadcast.md`}
        >
          complete first-broadcast guide
        </a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Diagnose, update and roll back</h2>

      <pre><code>{`sudo /opt/flowcast/scripts/community/doctor.sh
sudo /opt/flowcast/scripts/community/backup.sh
${updateCommand}`}</code></pre>

      <p>
        Back up before every version change. The update
        tooling preserves the installation’s credentials,
        persistent volumes and explicit Docker Control
        choice, subject to the release-specific compatibility
        notes.
      </p>

      <p>
        Use the documented backup and restore path for
        deliberate recovery or rollback. Preview releases do
        not guarantee downgrade-compatible persisted state.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <a
            href={`${repository}/blob/main/docs/community/update-rollback.md`}
          >
            Update and rollback
          </a>
        </li>

        <li>
          <a
            href={`${repository}/blob/main/docs/community/backup-restore.md`}
          >
            Backup and restore
          </a>
        </li>

        <li>
          <a
            href={`${repository}/blob/main/docs/community/known-limitations.md`}
          >
            Known limitations
          </a>
        </li>

        <li>
          <a
            href={`${repository}/blob/main/SECURITY.md`}
          >
            Security policy
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
